<p>Looks like it&#8217;s going to be one of <em>those</em> weeks. ￼<a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-gives-ipad-mini-its-biggest-update-ever/">Apple Newsroom:</a></p>
<blockquote><p>
  Apple today unveiled the all-new <a href="https://www.apple.com/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a>, featuring a stunning OLED display in an even thinner and lighter design, a huge leap in performance with A20 Pro, and water and dust resistance. The larger 8.5-inch OLED display, also available with a nano-texture option, delivers higher contrast and more than 2x higher peak brightness than the previous-generation iPad mini.
</p></blockquote>
<p>The OLED display is really the top-line new feature here, although of course a processor three generations newer will dramatically boost performance. It&#8217;s the first iPad mini with real water resistance, which Apple chalks up to a new feature called the Acoustic Display, in which audio is being channeled through the display surface rather than more porous speakers.</p>
<p>The starting price is now $699 for a binned Wi-Fi-only version. That&#8217;s not cheap, but also not as expensive as I feared. Fans of <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/10/is-the-beloved-ipad-mini-the-best-ipad/">this beloved model</a> will particularly love the idea of using the new nano-texture option, I suspect. ￼</p>
